      "id": "document:docs/agent-onboarding.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "agent-onboarding.md",
      "filePath": "docs/agent-onboarding.md",
      "summary": "Per-agent MCP onboarding reference (generated by `pactify agent docs`) describing how to wire the pact MCP server into nine agent surfaces — antigravity, claude-code, claude-desktop, codex-app, codex-cli, cursor-cli, gemini-cli, kimi-cli, opencode — with config file paths, entry blocks, and seat-id conventions.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "onboarding", "agent-integration", "mcp", "configuration"],
      "complexity": "complex"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:docs/architecture.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "architecture.md",
      "filePath": "docs/architecture.md",
      "summary": "Authoritative Pactify architecture document covering the .pact/ artifact layer, log.jsonl-as-event-bus comms (Phase 1 frozen), M3.4 best-effort relay interface, event schema, core design decisions (log-as-source, pull dispatch, role separation), the orchestrate driver, Phase 1 CLI commands, tech stack, open-core boundaries, and the layered Squad subsystems.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "architecture", "protocol", "design-decisions", "reference"],
      "complexity": "complex"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:docs/deployment.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "deployment.md",
      "filePath": "docs/deployment.md",
      "summary": "Pactify hosted deployment reference documenting the one-Vercel / two-Fly-apps topology split by git branch (main→staging→production fast-forward), CI gate (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`), planned install paths (Go/Node), per-project usage, dev environment notes, and the independently deployed pactify.dev Astro site split into its own repo with vendored sync.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "deployment", "ci-cd", "vercel", "fly-io"],
      "complexity": "moderate"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:docs/linx-coordination.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "linx-coordination.md",
      "filePath": "docs/linx-coordination.md",
      "summary": "Cross-team coordination checklist between Pactify and linx for sharing `@pactify-apps/relay` and `@pactify-apps/wire` during multi-machine orchestration (M2–M5), enumerating additive `RpcRequest` type extensions (zero linx code changes), the two auth-hardening items linx must implement (server-side challenge nonce, machine provisioning validation), optional pairing confirmation, and recommended coordination windows.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "coordination", "interop", "auth", "wire-protocol"],
      "complexity": "moderate"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:docs/onboarding.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "onboarding.md",
      "filePath": "docs/onboarding.md",
      "summary": "Five-minute project onboarding guide covering pactify installation, agent registration (machine-level), `pactify setup` project bootstrap, planner-driven task planning, `pactify orchestrate` autonomous execution, `pactify finish --pr` delivery, seat-definition semantics (`id:roles:entry[:kind]`), and dashboard deployment with Cloudflare Tunnel + Access for public exposure.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "onboarding", "getting-started", "cli", "tutorial"],
      "complexity": "moderate"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:docs/operations.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "operations.md",
      "filePath": "docs/operations.md",
      "summary": "Pactify day-2 operations reference covering daily dev workflow (`git pull` + `.agent/CURRENT.md`), troubleshooting (STATE.yml/log.jsonl drift, status-transition rules), relay enable/monitor/disable procedures using flags/env/Keychain, release flow (`./scripts/release.sh`), `pactify orchestrate` configuration (seat→kind, `verify:`, project gate, escalation), the manual half-auto alternative, and the coordination-authority P3 base-write contract.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "operations", "release", "orchestrate", "relay"],
      "complexity": "moderate"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:docs/plugin-publishing.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "plugin-publishing.md",
      "filePath": "docs/plugin-publishing.md",
      "summary": "Maintainer-only manual for the `pact` Claude plugin covering three testing/release paths (local `--plugin-dir` dev load, self-hosted `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` one-click install, optional personal skills dir), a pact-plugin-specific test checklist, and the deferred Anthropic community-marketplace submission procedure, with explicit reminders about `PACT_AGENT_ID` inheritance and version alignment in `plugins/pact/.claude-plugin/plugin.json`.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "plugin", "publishing", "claude", "marketplace"],
      "complexity": "moderate"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:docs/release-process.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "release-process.md",
      "filePath": "docs/release-process.md",
      "summary": "Trunk-based release process for the Pactify product (relay + Mission Control) using three fast-forward-only long-lived branches (`main` → `staging` → `production`), with explicit promote-and-deploy steps (Fly `relay`, Vercel preview/prod), shared-Neon branch separation, rollback via parent SHA, linx coordination rules, and a one-time Vercel/Fly/Neon setup checklist.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "release", "deployment", "promotion", "rollback"],
      "complexity": "moderate"
    }
  ],
